# Waystack Workbench — Implementation Plan v2 (reviewed, critiqued, phased)

> Supersedes `implementation_plan.md`. The product vision is unchanged. What changed: scope is phased into shippable slices, the stack is free-tier, authorization moves into the database, the security spec is fixed where it was unsafe, and every phase has tasks plus acceptance criteria.

---

## 0. Decisions locked from review

| # | Decision | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| D1 | Delivery | **Vertical slices** (Phase 0→7) | The original is ~6 products in one pass. Every phase ends in something deployable. |
| D2 | Backend / hosting | **Supabase free (Auth + Postgres + RLS + Edge Functions) + Cloudflare Pages (static host)** | Free, relational (orgs/shares need joins), RLS enforces tenancy in the DB, Google sign-in built in. Cloud SQL is paid and always-on. Vercel Hobby forbids commercial use, so Pages is safer for the SaaS path. |
| D3 | AI Studio role | **Use AI Studio Build to scaffold UI/components only**; backend is Supabase via the public anon key | AI Studio's built-in backend integration is Firebase-oriented (verify current state). Org/share data is relational, so Postgres wins. Firebase Auth + Firestore is the fallback if you want 100% AI Studio-native, at the cost of rewriting sharing as Firestore rules. |
| D4 | Rust | **Rust→Wasm in a Web Worker, only for the hot paths (secret scanning, big-log filtering). Everything else is TypeScript.** Every Wasm function has a TS reference implementation behind the same interface. | Keeps your Rust goal where it measurably pays; the TS fallback keeps the app working if Wasm fails to load, and doubles as the test oracle. |
| D5 | Ruby | **Not used** | `ruby.wasm` is tens of MB, there is no server need, and it adds a third language for zero benefit. Revisit only for a CLI/gem. |
| D6 | Audience | **Three launch tiers on one codebase** (see §11): A Portfolio → B Team → C Public SaaS. Nothing is dropped; each tier adds gates. | You want all three. |
| D7 | Name | **Waystack** (working name; see §20) | Kairn is taken. |
| D8 | Sign-in | Google + GitHub + email | Both requested. |
| D9 | Voiceover | None; captions only | Requested. |
| D10 | **Budget** | **$0. Nothing in this plan may require payment, a card on file, or a paid plan.** | Hard constraint; see §21. Where a feature would cost money it is cut, replaced, or deferred. |

Known free-tier limits to design around: Supabase free pauses after ~7 days of inactivity, has 500 MB DB, and has no managed backups. So: add a keep-alive cron, ship user **Export all (JSON)**, and run a weekly `pg_dump` via GitHub Actions, **encrypted with `age` before it is stored** (dumps contain user data; use a private repo's artifacts, never a public repo's). See §21.

