## 2. Verified facts about adopted repos (checked this session)

- **`heygen-com/hyperframes`** exists (HTML→MP4, headless Chrome + FFmpeg, Node ≥ 22). Most sources say **Apache-2.0**, but one mirror claims a custom license, so **read the official `LICENSE` before shipping**. It is built for agents (`npx skills add heygen-com/hyperframes`). MP4 rendering is a CLI step; an in-browser player has to be built on its composition format or kept simple (see §8).
- **`Nutlope/hallmark`** exists as an anti-slop design skill with a dependency-free `scripts/sloplint.mjs` checker and a ~57–58 gate slop-test. **Action:** run `sloplint` in CI against built HTML instead of re-implementing its rules in this plan. Confirm its actual rules from the repo, not from this document.
- **`vercel-labs/agent-browser`** (Apache-2.0, Rust CLI) takes **accessibility-tree snapshots of a live browser page** with `@e1`-style refs that go stale after DOM changes. It does **not** convert pasted HTML. Waystack's "paste HTML → `@ref` wireframe" is therefore **our own re-implementation** (parse HTML → keep interactive/semantic nodes → assign refs). Spec it that way (§7.1).

