## 3. Stack and repo layout

- **Frontend**: Vite + React + TypeScript (strict), React Router, TanStack Query, Zustand (UI state only), Radix UI primitives, CSS variables for tokens (Tailwind optional). Scaffold with AI Studio Build, then own the code in git.
- **Backend**: Supabase (Auth, Postgres 15+, RLS, Storage unused for now, Edge Functions on Deno for `proxy` and `mcp`).
- **Host**: Cloudflare Pages (free, commercial use OK). Edge Functions on Supabase.
- **Wasm**: Rust crate built with `wasm-pack --target web`, loaded in a dedicated Worker via `comlink`.
- **Tests**: Vitest (unit), Playwright (e2e + a11y via `@axe-core/playwright`), pgTAP or SQL tests for RLS, `cargo test` for Rust.
- **CI**: GitHub Actions (typecheck, lint, test, `sloplint`, build, size budget, Lighthouse CI).

```
waystack/
  apps/web/                 # Vite app
    src/{shell,apps/{packer,runner,explorer,composer},vault,orgs,mcp,docs,design}/
  packages/
    core/                   # TS interfaces + TS reference impls (scrub, tokens, regex, template)
    wasm-engine/            # Rust crate -> wasm, same interfaces as core
    ui/                     # tokens, Button, InputField, InfoPopover, SplitPane, AppCard...
  supabase/
    migrations/             # SQL (schema + RLS), numbered
    functions/{proxy,mcp}/  # Edge Functions
    tests/                  # RLS tests
  content/tutorials/        # HyperFrames compositions per app
  docs/                     # ADRs, threat model
```

