## 7. App specs

### 7.1 App 1 — AI Context Packer & Privacy Firewall
- **Input**: drag a folder (File System Access API / `webkitdirectory`), a `.zip` (`fflate`), or pasted text/HTML. No server reads. (GitHub URL import = later, via the proxy.)
- **Processing (all local, in a Worker)**: ignore rules (`.gitignore`, defaults), binary skip, size cap (default 5 MB total, configurable), output formats (XML-ish, Markdown, plain), per-file headers.
- **Scrubbing**: rule set (AWS keys, GCP keys, GitHub/Slack/Stripe tokens, JWT, Bearer, private-key blocks, emails, IPv4/6, high-entropy strings) from a versioned JSON list; the Wasm `RegexSet` engine plus the TS fallback; each hit shows the rule, line, and masked preview, and the user can **allow/deny per hit**; diff view before copy.
- **Tokens**: "≈ tokens" per file and total, tokenizer selector; budget meter with the largest-files list and "drop file" action.
- **`@ref` wireframe mode (own implementation)**: parse HTML with `DOMParser`; keep landmarks, headings, links, buttons, inputs (with labels), text; drop script/style/svg paths/hidden; assign stable ordered refs `@e1 [button] "Sign in"`; output a compact text tree; show a before/after token count. Document that refs are **only meaningful for the pasted snapshot**.
- **Outputs**: copy, download, save to Vault, "Expose as MCP tool" (Phase 7).

### 7.2 App 2 — Visual API & Webhook Runner
- Steps: method, URL, headers, body; variables from earlier steps via **JSONPath** (`{{steps.login.body$.token}}`); a restricted template syntax (no code eval); secret variables stored encrypted/in Vault and masked in UI and logs; cycle and missing-reference errors shown inline.
- Waterfall (DNS/connect/TLS/wait/download where the proxy can measure), headers, body viewer (JSON tree, truncation notice), and a console-style error inspector (status ≥ 400, timeouts, invalid JSON) with plain-English hints.
- Run modes: browser-direct, or via the proxy (clearly indicated). Cancel button. Per-run caps (steps ≤ 20, total time ≤ 60 s).
- Import curl / export curl and `.http` file.

### 7.3 App 3 — Log, Regex & Cron Explorer
- **Logs**: drop a file (stream-read in chunks, up to ~200 MB), filter by text/regex/level/time, virtualized list (`@tanstack/react-virtual`), Wasm line filter for large files (TS fallback below a threshold), JSON-lines detection and field facets.
- **Regex**: native JS flavor, live match and capture-group highlighting, `regexp-tree` for an explanation, a catastrophic-backtracking warning (timeout in a Worker), test-case table; "Rust flavor" tab (Wasm) with a diff of differences from JS.
- **Cron**: `cronstrue` for plain English, `cron-parser` for the next 10 runs, timezone selector, 5-field and Quartz variants flagged.

### 7.4 App 4 — Template & Prompt Composer
- `{{variable}}` templates; auto-generated fill-in form (types: text, long text, select, number); live split-pane preview; missing-variable highlighting; escape syntax documented.
- **Specification Distiller presets**: static preset templates inspired by `pbakaus/impeccable` commands (distill, clarify, polish, harden, adapt), stored as JSON, loaded lazily. Check that repo's license before copying any wording; otherwise write original presets.
- Save template to Vault (personal/org), share, version, annotate.

### 7.5 Design system and tokens
- Semantic tokens only in components (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--border-subtle`, `--text`, `--text-muted`, `--accent`, `--success`, `--warning`, `--danger`), mapped per theme. The four palettes from v1 stay; each must pass **WCAG AA** (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large text/UI) in a build-time contrast check.
- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans + JetBrains Mono (`tabular-nums`), self-hosted, `font-display: swap`.
- Density and motion are CSS variables; `prefers-reduced-motion` forces Reduced.
- Component rules: 1 card level, hairline dividers, focus ring visible in all themes, hit targets ≥ 40 px (44 on touch).
- Gate: `sloplint` in CI plus manual review against the Hallmark slop-test.

