## 10. Testing, CI, observability

### 10.1 Layers
- Unit (Vitest): scrub rules (labeled corpus, recall/precision report), token counting, template engine, JSONPath chaining, cron/regex helpers. **Property-based tests** (fast-check) for the template engine and encryption round trip.
- Rust: `cargo test` plus a **differential test** (Wasm vs TS reference over the same corpus; the outputs must be identical).
- DB: SQL tests for RLS (pgTAP or a Vitest harness using several JWTs).
- E2E (Playwright): guest save → sign in → import; org invite → accept → shared item; share → revoke; encrypted item round trip; proxy blocked-URL cases; theme persistence; keyboard-only run of the main flows.
- A11y: axe on every route in every theme; manual screen reader pass (NVDA/VoiceOver) before Tier B.
- Perf: Lighthouse CI (LCP < 2.5 s on throttled mobile for Home), bundle budgets, a Wasm load-time check.

### 10.2 RLS test matrix (must be green before Phase 2 merges)
Actors: owner, admin, member, outsider, view-sharee, edit-sharee, unverified-email user, anon.
Actions: select, insert, update, delete, share, annotate, change `owner_id`/`org_id`, read versions, read audit log.
Every cell has an expected allow/deny, asserted in code.

### 10.3 Observability
Sentry free tier (frontend errors, scrub PII), Supabase logs for Edge Functions, a `/health` Edge Function plus an uptime ping (UptimeRobot free), structured logs without bodies or secrets.

### 10.4 CI pipeline
install → typecheck → lint → unit → Rust tests + wasm build → RLS tests (local Supabase) → build → `sloplint` → axe e2e → size budget → deploy preview to Cloudflare Pages. Main branch → production deploy; migrations applied via `supabase db push` in a gated job.

