- **Concept:** a trail marker built from stacked stones: a way to find your path through complex terrain.
- **Working name: Waystack** (waymark + stack). Reasons: short, easy to say, ties to the stone-stack emblem, reads as developer tooling. Web searches found no product by that name, but this is **not** legal clearance.
- **Alternates:** Cairnbench (closest to the old idea, but "cairn" is crowded: several projects and a language use it), Talusbench (talus = loose stones on a slope; distinctive but harder to spell).
- **Clearance checklist before building the brand (do on Day 0):**
  1. Check USPTO TESS/TMSearch and EUIPO for "Waystack" in software classes 9, 42.
  2. Search GitHub org/user, npm, PyPI, crates.io, Product Hunt, and Google for exact matches.
  3. Domains: check `.com`, `.dev`, `.app`; buy through your registrar; only you can pay. Pick the final name only if the `.com` or `.dev` plus the GitHub org and npm scope are free.
  4. If anything conflicts, fall back to the next alternate and re-run.
- **Rename cost:** the brand string lives in one `brand.ts` constant, the SVG emblem component, the token prefix (`way_`), and the package scope, so a rename is cheap if done before launch.

## 21. $0 budget guardrails (hard constraint)

**Rule:** no feature may need money, a credit card, or a paid tier. Limits below are as I understand current free tiers; **they change, so re-check each vendor page on Day 0** and record the date in `docs/free-tier-limits.md`.

| Need | $0 choice | Catch and how the plan handles it |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend host | Cloudflare Pages (free) | No card. Use the free `*.pages.dev` address. |
| Database + auth | Supabase free | Pauses after ~7 days idle; 500 MB; no managed backups. Keep-alive cron + encrypted weekly dump (below) + user export. |
| Server code | Supabase Edge Functions (free quota) | Quota cap, see usage caps below. |
| CI, cron, backups | GitHub Actions | Free minutes. Public repos are unlimited; private repos have a monthly cap. Keep the repo public **and never put dumps in it** (encrypt, see below), or keep it private and watch minutes. |
| Errors / uptime | Sentry free, UptimeRobot free | Small quotas; scrub PII; sample events. |
| Bot protection | Cloudflare Turnstile (free) | Needs a free Cloudflare account. |
| OAuth | Google Cloud OAuth client, GitHub OAuth app | Free; Google needs **no billing account** for sign-in only. |
| MP4 tutorials | HyperFrames + FFmpeg run in GitHub Actions | Free. |
| Video/poster hosting | Committed to the repo / Pages (keep each file small) | Pages has per-file and per-site size limits; keep clips short and compressed. |
| Email | **Avoid sending email** | Supabase's built-in email is heavily rate-limited, and free third-party senders need a domain you'd have to buy. So: (1) OAuth (Google/GitHub) is the primary sign-in; (2) **org invites and shares use a copyable link**, not email; (3) email/password sign-up is optional and gated behind a feature flag, with confirmation mails limited to a few per hour: fine for a demo, not for strangers. |
| Domain | **Free `*.pages.dev`** | A custom domain is the one unavoidable cost (~$10/yr); it is **deferred** and not required for any tier. |
| Pen-test, legal counsel, paid SMTP, billing processor, Pro plans | **Cut** | Replaced by the self-audit checklist (§6, §10), free policy templates, link-based invites, and "no billing". |

**Backups at $0:** a scheduled GitHub Action runs `pg_dump`, encrypts with `age` (public key in the repo, private key only on your machine), and uploads as a private-repo artifact (kept ~90 days). Do a restore drill once into a throwaway local Supabase.

**Usage caps so a free tier can never turn into a bill or an outage:**
- `MAX_USERS` env var checked at sign-up (default 100); beyond it, a "waitlist" screen.
- `PROXY_ENABLED` and `MCP_ENABLED` kill-switch env vars; per-user daily proxy limit (default 100/day) and a **global** daily limit so abuse can't burn the Edge Function quota.
- Quotas from §17 enforced in the database. At 80% of DB size an owner alert appears in the admin page; at 95% new writes are refused (read and export still work).
- Nothing in the app is allowed to call a metered API (no LLM calls, no paid maps/email/SMS). The MCP router is keyword-based for exactly this reason.

**What this changes in the plan:** no custom SMTP, no paid pen-test, no Supabase Pro, no billing, no custom domain, no external status page service, no paid error tracking. **Upgrade path when you someday want money-based features:** custom domain first, then email sender, then Pro; §16 describes the order.

**Spend-safety check for every new dependency/service:** "Does it work with no card on file, forever, at 10x my expected traffic, and what happens at its limit?" If the answer is a bill, it does not go in.
